  "summary": "Full assessment of all 1,395 English/Vietnamese passages: chapter headings 1–12 and every paragraph, from the narrator’s opening note to the departure from Herland. The first reviews scored 8.65, 8.35, 8.30 and 8.375 across four ranges and found five majors (misread senses, an aircraft written as a balloon, idioms that flipped); three further rounds of fixes and fresh separate-context reviews found six more majors (two flipped idioms, a mistaken ‘breed out’, and ‘bi-sexual’ rendered three times as ‘lưỡng tính’), all corrected, and the flattened em-dashes were restored. The last fresh reviews scored 8.80 (units 1–390), 8.725 (391–735), 8.725 (736–1070) and 8.675 (1071–1395) with no major or critical finding, and the remaining minor points were then applied. The final score is taken from the weakest range, 8.675 on the half-point scale, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
